# Performance Optimization Guidelines for AWallet

## 🎯 MOBILE PERFORMANCE PRINCIPLES

Mobile devices have constraints that web apps don't:
- **Limited CPU/GPU** - Less processing power
- **Limited Memory** - App can be killed if using too much
- **Battery Constraints** - Inefficient code drains battery
- **Network Variability** - Users may have slow/unstable connections

## 🚫 PERFORMANCE - NEVER DO

### Critical Performance Mistakes:
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER - Inline object/array in render
function BadComponent() {
  return (
    <View style={{ padding: 10, margin: 5 }}>
      <FlatList data={[1, 2, 3]} />
    </View>
  );
}

// ❌ NEVER - Create functions in render
function BadComponent() {
  return (
    <Pressable onPress={() => console.log('pressed')}>
      <Child onEvent={(x) => handleEvent(x)} />
    </Pressable>
  );
}

// ❌ NEVER - Expensive calculations in render
function BadComponent({ items }) {
  const sorted = items.sort((a, b) => a - b); // Runs every render!
  return <View />;
}

// ❌ NEVER - Deep object comparisons in useEffect deps
useEffect(() => {
  doSomething();
}, [largeObject]); // Will re-run on every render!

// ❌ NEVER - Synchronous expensive operations on UI thread
function BadComponent() {
  const processedData = heavyComputation(bigDataSet); // Blocks UI!
  return <View />;
}
```

## ✅ PERFORMANCE - ALWAYS DO

### Memoization Strategy:
```typescript
// ✅ useMemo for expensive calculations
import { useMemo } from 'react';

function GoodComponent({ items }) {
  const sortedItems = useMemo(() => {
    return items.sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price);
  }, [items]);
  
  const statistics = useMemo(() => {
    return {
      total: items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0),
      average: items.length > 0 ? total / items.length : 0,
    };
  }, [items]);
  
  return <View>{/* Use sortedItems and statistics */}</View>;
}

// ✅ useCallback for functions passed to children
function GoodComponent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  
  const handleIncrement = useCallback(() => {
    setCount(c => c + 1);
  }, []);
  
  const handleDecrement = useCallback(() => {
    setCount(c => c - 1);
  }, []);
  
  return (
    <>
      <MemoizedButton onPress={handleIncrement}>+</MemoizedButton>
      <MemoizedButton onPress={handleDecrement}>-</MemoizedButton>
    </>
  );
}

// ✅ React.memo for components that re-render often
export const ExpensiveChild = React.memo(({ data, onAction }) => {
  // Expensive rendering logic
  return <View>{/* ... */}</View>;
});
```

### List Performance:
```typescript
import { FlatList, VirtualizedList } from 'react-native';

// ✅ Use FlatList for long lists
function GoodListComponent({ items }) {
  const renderItem = useCallback(({ item }) => (
    <ItemComponent item={item} />
  ), []);
  
  const keyExtractor = useCallback((item) => item.id, []);
  
  return (
    <FlatList
      data={items}
      renderItem={renderItem}
      keyExtractor={keyExtractor}
      // Performance optimizations
      removeClippedSubviews={true}
      maxToRenderPerBatch={10}
      updateCellsBatchingPeriod={50}
      initialNumToRender={10}
      windowSize={21}
      getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({
        length: ITEM_HEIGHT,
        offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,
        index,
      })}
    />
  );
}

// ❌ WRONG - map() for long lists
function BadListComponent({ items }) {
  return (
    <ScrollView>
      {items.map(item => <ItemComponent key={item.id} item={item} />)}
    </ScrollView>
  );
}
```

### Image Optimization:
```typescript
import { Image } from 'expo-image';

// ✅ Use expo-image (faster, better caching)
function GoodImageComponent({ source }) {
  return (
    <Image
      source={source}
      placeholder={blurhash}
      contentFit="cover"
      transition={1000}
      cachePolicy="memory-disk"
    />
